# Kivali Desktop guest. PID 1 is busybox init: it reaps orphans,
# runs `boot` to completion, then starts k3s, the readiness reporter
# and the data disk trim (after READY, then daily) once each, keeps the
# guest agent (vsock, for kivali-supervisor) and the console control
# loop (the only reader of the console) running, and runs `shutdown`
# before powering off.
::sysinit:/usr/libexec/kivali/boot
::once:/usr/libexec/kivali/k3s-server
::once:/usr/libexec/kivali/ready
::once:/usr/libexec/kivali/trim
::respawn:/usr/libexec/kivali/guest-agent
::respawn:/usr/libexec/kivali/console-control
::shutdown:/usr/libexec/kivali/shutdown
